  "File": "src/app/(app)/studio/components/StudioPreviewPanel.preview-url.test.tsx",
  "SymlinkFile": "",
  "Commit": "6b34d5d1859f082b0a569eb7cbd854d5a35eec1d",
  "Link": "https://github.com/LabsConnected/litlabs-website/blob/6b34d5d1859f082b0a569eb7cbd854d5a35eec1d/src/app/(app)/studio/components/StudioPreviewPanel.preview-url.test.tsx#L36",
  "Entropy": 3.8413284,
  "Author": "Larry's LiTT",
  "Email": "highlife4real1989@gmail.com",
  "Date": "2026-09-21T07:56:02Z",
  "Message": "fix: Studio preview URL hardening + transient-302 fingerprint logging\n\n- buildPreviewProxyUrl strips trailing slashes from the terminal base URL\n  so it can never produce //preview/... (Express would miss the route)\n- Regression tests: preview URL never collapses to the bare terminal root,\n  PREVIEW_PROXY_HOST keeps path+token, trailing-slash base keeps token,\n  iframe src contract pinned end to end\n- Temporary diagnostic logging in terminal-server preview proxy: fingerprint\n  any upstream 3xx (exact Location, rewritten target, server headers) to\n  identify the transient 02:30 302 emitter if it recurs. Additive only,\n  no behavior change; safe to remove once the emitter is found.",
  "Tags": [],
  "Fingerprint": "6b34d5d1859f082b0a569eb7cbd854d5a35eec1d:src/app/(app)/studio/components/StudioPreviewPanel.preview-url.test.tsx:generic-api-key:36"
 },
 {
  "RuleID": "stripe-access-token",
  "Description": "Found a Stripe Access Token, posing a risk to payment processing services and sensitive financial data.",
  "StartLine": 153,
  "EndLine": 153,
  "StartColumn": 46,
  "EndColumn": 64,
  "Match": "REDACTED\"",
  "Secret": "REDACTED",
  "File": "terminal-server/__tests__/preview-manager.test.ts",
  "SymlinkFile": "",
  "Commit": "235fc706032c12b36590ef0deceee0b7a0e67a76",
  "Link": "https://github.com/LabsConnected/litlabs-website/blob/235fc706032c12b36590ef0deceee0b7a0e67a76/terminal-server/__tests__/preview-manager.test.ts#L153",
  "Entropy": 3.308271,
  "Author": "Litree-Ceo",
  "Email": "litbi@homebase.local",
  "Date": "2026-09-21T07:40:17Z",
  "Message": "fix(preview): never inject platform Clerk secret into workspace children\n\nCLERK_SECRET_KEY, CLERK_PUBLISHABLE_KEY, and\nNEXT_PUBLIC_CLERK_PUBLISHABLE_KEY are removed from the preview env\nallowlist entirely — the platform's own Clerk app can never reach\nuntrusted generated code, and its publishable key can no longer shadow\na workspace's own .env.local pair.\n\nPreview auth is preserved through an isolated credential path:\nPREVIEW_CLERK_SECRET_KEY / PREVIEW_CLERK_PUBLISHABLE_KEY (a dedicated\npreview Clerk app) are mapped onto the standard CLERK_* names, and a\nworkspace's own .env* files — which the dev server loads itself — now\nsatisfy validateClerkConfig via readWorkspaceEnvFiles().\n\nThe secret-name guard now runs before PREVIEW_ENV_ALLOWLIST, so the ops\nallowlist can only admit benign names, and the never-pass list gains\nCLERK_SECRET_KEY, DATABASE_URL, and SUPABASE service-role/secret keys.\n\nGenerated with [Devin](https://devin.ai)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Devin \u003c158243242+devin-ai-integration[bot]@users.noreply.github.com\u003e",
  "Tags": [],
  "Fingerprint": "235fc706032c12b36590ef0deceee0b7a0e67a76:terminal-server/__tests__/preview-manager.test.ts:stripe-access-token:153"
 },
