  "Commit": "235fc706032c12b36590ef0deceee0b7a0e67a76",
  "Link": "https://github.com/LabsConnected/litlabs-website/blob/235fc706032c12b36590ef0deceee0b7a0e67a76/terminal-server/__tests__/preview-manager.test.ts#L915",
  "Entropy": 4.121928,
  "Author": "Litree-Ceo",
  "Email": "litbi@homebase.local",
  "Date": "2026-09-21T07:40:17Z",
  "Message": "fix(preview): never inject platform Clerk secret into workspace children\n\nCLERK_SECRET_KEY, CLERK_PUBLISHABLE_KEY, and\nNEXT_PUBLIC_CLERK_PUBLISHABLE_KEY are removed from the preview env\nallowlist entirely — the platform's own Clerk app can never reach\nuntrusted generated code, and its publishable key can no longer shadow\na workspace's own .env.local pair.\n\nPreview auth is preserved through an isolated credential path:\nPREVIEW_CLERK_SECRET_KEY / PREVIEW_CLERK_PUBLISHABLE_KEY (a dedicated\npreview Clerk app) are mapped onto the standard CLERK_* names, and a\nworkspace's own .env* files — which the dev server loads itself — now\nsatisfy validateClerkConfig via readWorkspaceEnvFiles().\n\nThe secret-name guard now runs before PREVIEW_ENV_ALLOWLIST, so the ops\nallowlist can only admit benign names, and the never-pass list gains\nCLERK_SECRET_KEY, DATABASE_URL, and SUPABASE service-role/secret keys.\n\nGenerated with [Devin](https://devin.ai)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Devin \u003c158243242+devin-ai-integration[bot]@users.noreply.github.com\u003e",
  "Tags": [],
  "Fingerprint": "235fc706032c12b36590ef0deceee0b7a0e67a76:terminal-server/__tests__/preview-manager.test.ts:generic-api-key:915"
 },
