  "Message": "fix(terminal-server): validate Clerk config before preview spawn, surface auth errors truthfully\n\nThe preview runtime inherits the terminal-server's process.env. If the\nterminal-server has a stale or malformed CLERK_SECRET_KEY, the preview's\nClerk middleware crashes with a 500 (\"secret-key-invalid\") that manifests\nas a generic 60-second \"Dev server did not become healthy\" timeout.\n\nChanges:\n- validateClerkConfig() runs BEFORE spawning the dev server, checking:\n  presence, prefix (sk_test_/sk_live_ for secret, pk_test_/pk_live_ for\n  publishable), key mismatch, and test/live environment mismatch\n- CLERK_PUBLISHABLE_KEY to NEXT_PUBLIC_CLERK_PUBLISHABLE_KEY fallback mapping\n  (the var name @clerk/nextjs expects)\n- cleanEnvValue() strips whitespace/newlines/quotes from Railway copy-paste\n- fingerprintClerkEnv() logs a redacted SHA-256 fingerprint (prefix + length\n  + hash only, never the full key value)\n- probeHealth() now detects 5xx auth config errors and surfaces\n  preview_auth_config_error instead of a generic timeout\n- server.ts propagates errorCode in the 500 response so Studio can show\n  the real failure reason\n\nNew error codes: preview_clerk_config_error, preview_auth_config_error\n\nProduction terminal-server currently has:\n- CLERK_SECRET_KEY: PRESENT (sk_live_, valid)\n- CLERK_PUBLISHABLE_KEY: PRESENT (pk_live_, valid)\n- NEXT_PUBLIC_CLERK_PUBLISHABLE_KEY: ABSENT\nThe fallback mapping fixes this without requiring a Railway env change.\n\nGenerated with [Devin](https://devin.ai)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Devin \u003c158243242+devin-ai-integration[bot]@users.noreply.github.com\u003e",
