  "Secret": "REDACTED",
  "File": "src/lib/deployments/user-deployment.test.ts",
  "SymlinkFile": "",
  "Commit": "1a5bfda056cbd761310c5876838079af4c6f697a",
  "Link": "https://github.com/LabsConnected/litlabs-website/blob/1a5bfda056cbd761310c5876838079af4c6f697a/src/lib/deployments/user-deployment.test.ts#L234",
  "Entropy": 3.8521688,
  "Author": "Larry B",
  "Email": "highlife4real1989@gmail.com",
  "Date": "2026-09-13T03:24:25Z",
  "Message": "feat(v1): user-project deploy capability + truthful completion semantics\n\nTwo V1 blockers, both found from production Ember Roast evidence.\n\n1. FALSE COMPLETION — \"Work log · 1 of 1 steps complete\" appeared for a\n   conversational reply that called no tool and changed nothing. Four\n   independent layers each produced this:\n\n   - StudioTranscript counted `message.actions?.length ?? 1`, so any\n     assistant text rendered as one completed step — and `actions` are\n     PROPOSED canvas actions, not work that happened.\n   - The message route's `status: \"completed\"` means \"stream finished\";\n     the UI read it as \"work finished\".\n   - agent-loop-v2 defaulted finalText to \"I've completed the requested\n     work\" when the model returned nothing.\n   - intent-router classified \"Build me a website for Ember Roast\" as\n     `think`/requiresExecution:false, routing a build request to the\n     read-only loop where it could only be discussed.\n\n   Completion is now judged from evidence (completion-evidence.ts): a\n   build needs a successful mutating tool result; a deploy needs a\n   verified live URL. No evidence renders NO work log.\n\n2. NO USER-PROJECT DEPLOY — the V2 loop had no tool able to deploy the\n   user's project, so build → preview → deploy live → live URL could not\n   complete. `preview.open` is registered but disabled (no handler),\n   CLI `project.ship` is git shipping, and /api/deploy/trigger redeploys\n   LiTT's OWN admin-gated Railway service.\n\n   Adds `project.deploy`: collects the workspace's static output, stores\n   an immutable snapshot, serves it publicly at /sites/\u003cid\u003e/, and fetches\n   that URL before reporting ready. Identity comes from the authorized\n   WorkspaceTransport — no tenant, project, provider or service inputs —\n   so it cannot target another user's project or LiTT infrastructure.\n\nAlso fixed, found while testing:\n- AUTO mode SKIPPED approval-requiring tools instead of asking the user,\n  making any sensitive action unreachable in AUTO. It now pauses for\n  approval exactly as ACT does (AUTO still never exceeds ACT privilege).\n- A provider failure after a successful deployment lost the live URL and\n  invited a duplicate deploy; the closing text now reports it.\n- run_project_checks reported git/tsc/eslint as FAILED on static\n  no-repository workspaces; now classified not_applicable.\n- previewStatus was fabricated from workspace verification, so a ready\n  workspace implied a running preview.\n\nTests: 12 behavioural cases (A-L) across artifact safety, authorization,\nduplicate suppression, URL verification, loop continuation, and\npreview/deployment separation.\n\nNOTE: supabase/migrations/20260912230000_add_project_deployments.sql is\nNOT yet applied to any database. project.deploy will fail truthfully\n(\"Deployment storage is unavailable\") until it is.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) \u003cnoreply@anthropic.com\u003e\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UhG2soAaZZE6P6Bz2Vj9cc",
  "Tags": [],
  "Fingerprint": "1a5bfda056cbd761310c5876838079af4c6f697a:src/lib/deployments/user-deployment.test.ts:generic-api-key:234"
 },
