  "Commit": "ca55bc9c9d890d5a9e4ae253abd274065f1a5e43",
  "Link": "https://github.com/LabsConnected/litlabs-website/blob/ca55bc9c9d890d5a9e4ae253abd274065f1a5e43/src/lib/litt-intelligence/llm-tool-calling.test.ts#L544",
  "Entropy": 3.75,
  "Author": "Larry Bol",
  "Email": "laidbacknostress4life@gmail.com",
  "Date": "2026-09-13T01:11:01Z",
  "Message": "feat(llm): add resilient Basic provider router and failover\n\nProvider-neutral tool-calling runtime for Basic users. Routes requests\nthrough a registry-planned sequence — Gemini direct, OpenRouter free,\nGroq, Mistral, Cloudflare Workers AI, local Ollama — instead of depending\non OpenRouter alone. BYOK routes are user-funded only when the user\nsupplies a key; paid platform models are never auto-selected on Basic.\n\n- Per-provider circuit breaker with failure classification\n  (401/402/403/404/408/429/5xx/network) and Retry-After honoring\n- One shared absolute deadline across all provider attempts; budget\n  exhaustion surfaces truthfully instead of a generic failure\n- Agent transcript and tool state preserved across mid-run failover;\n  duplicate mutations are replayed, never re-executed\n- Sanitized, truthful user-facing failure text; no secrets in errors,\n  logs, or provider diagnostics\n- Studio reports the actual routed provider/model; Voice uses the same\n  shared deadline inside the Vapi response window\n- Safe /api/llm/health basicRoutes diagnostics (state only, no keys)\n\nGenerated with [Devin](https://devin.ai)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Devin \u003c158243242+devin-ai-integration[bot]@users.noreply.github.com\u003e",
  "Tags": [],
  "Fingerprint": "ca55bc9c9d890d5a9e4ae253abd274065f1a5e43:src/lib/litt-intelligence/llm-tool-calling.test.ts:generic-api-key:544"
 },
