  "File": ".git-commit-msg.txt",
  "SymlinkFile": "",
  "Commit": "82497b09964e51ff0aae8db62d193acbc3fa7a0e",
  "Link": "https://github.com/LabsConnected/litlabs-website/blob/82497b09964e51ff0aae8db62d193acbc3fa7a0e/.git-commit-msg.txt#L6",
  "Entropy": 3.75,
  "Author": "Laid-Back-89",
  "Email": "highlife4real1989@gmail.com",
  "Date": "2026-09-07T01:42:26Z",
  "Message": "Clerk/OAuth cleanup: retire accounts.litlabs.net, add release guard (#150)\n\n* Clerk/OAuth cleanup: retire accounts.litlabs.net, add release guard\n\nConsolidates Clerk OAuth configuration around a single canonical setup:\n\nCANONICAL:\n- OAuth client_id: YWeGjVVwoNnX4RTY (PKCE public client, no secret)\n- Clerk FAPI / OAuth issuer: https://clerk.litlabs.net\n- OIDC issuer (from .well-known): https://litlabs.net/__clerk\n- OAuth consent: https://www.litlabs.net/oauth-consent\n- Sign-in: https://www.litlabs.net/sign-in (preserves redirect_url)\n- ClerkProvider: direct FAPI, no proxy (proxyUrl empty)\n\nRETIRED:\n- accounts.litlabs.net (old Account Portal) — no longer used for consent\n- The sign-in page rewrites any accounts.litlabs.net redirect_url to\n  www.litlabs.net as a defensive shim until the Clerk Dashboard is updated\n\nCHANGES:\n- oauth-consent/page.tsx: update comment, remove retired domain reference\n- inspect-consent-state.mjs: update response filter to www.litlabs.net\n- Add tests/auth-domain-release-guard.test.ts: fails if retired domains\n  leak into production source (with allowlist for the defensive rewrite)\n- Add debug/trace scripts for OAuth flow verification\n\nThe Clerk Dashboard OAuth client's consent URL must still be updated\nfrom accounts.litlabs.net/oauth-consent to www.litlabs.net/oauth-consent\n(requires Dashboard access — no API for this setting).\n\nGenerated with [Devin](https://devin.ai)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Devin \u003c158243242+devin-ai-integration[bot]@users.noreply.github.com\u003e\n\n* fix: redirect litlabs.net sign-in and oauth-consent to www.litlabs.net\n\nThe naked litlabs.net apex renders an empty/broken Clerk sign-in\n\npage because Clerk's session cookies and components are not\n\ncorrectly scoped there. Force a 308 redirect to www.litlabs.net\n\nfor /sign-in and /oauth-consent before Clerk middleware runs, so\n\nthe browser always signs in on the canonical application domain.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Devin \u003c158243242+devin-ai-integration[bot]@users.noreply.github.com\u003e",
  "Tags": [],
  "Fingerprint": "82497b09964e51ff0aae8db62d193acbc3fa7a0e:.git-commit-msg.txt:generic-api-key:6"
 },
