  "Message": "feat: observability/command-dispatch closure — one registry, one harness\n\nEstablishes a single command registry as the source of truth for all\nslash commands, with registry-derived dispatch, /doctor + /doctor --deep\nprobes (individually timeout-bounded), secret redaction, and a PID-tracked\ntest harness that kills only its spawned runtime.\n\nOne LiTT runtime truth. One command registry. One dispatch path. One test harness.\n\n- terminal-server/command-registry.ts: 14 commands with full metadata\n  (command, aliases, description, category, mutability, responseKind, handler).\n  /help, validation, and dispatch all derive from this registry.\n- terminal-server/doctor.ts: /doctor (4 fast probes) + /doctor --deep\n  (9 probes, each with its own timeout — one hanging probe cannot hang\n  the overall check). Statuses: PASS/WARN/FAIL/TIMEOUT/SKIP.\n- terminal-server/command-bridge.ts: refactored to dispatch via registry,\n  removed hardcoded SUPPORTED_COMMANDS list.\n- terminal-server/server.ts: /internal/command accepts slash commands,\n  unknown commands return controlled error (never crash).\n- tools/test-runtime.ps1: PID-tracked -KillOnExit harness. Kills ONLY\n  the spawned PID via taskkill /T /F /PID. Never uses Stop-Process -Name\n  or taskkill /IM. try/finally cleanup. Non-zero exit on failed gates.\n- tests/runtime-closure.test.ts: 42 tests covering registry integrity,\n  dispatch, doctor, secret redaction, and process safety contracts.\n\nClosure results:\n- Registered commands: 14. Harness checks/assertions: 26. All passed.\n- /doctor --deep: 8 PASS / 1 WARN / 0 FAIL / 0 TIMEOUT.\n- Observability closure failures: 0. Repository-wide typecheck still\n  has pre-existing failures in untouched files.\n- Safety audit: shell.ts and execution.ts use PID-specific process-tree\n  kills only — no broad process-name killing found.\n\nGenerated with [Devin](https://devin.ai)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Devin \u003c158243242+devin-ai-integration[bot]@users.noreply.g