  "Date": "2026-08-14T06:37:48Z",
  "Message": "feat(sec-4,sec-5): RuntimeApprovalProvider + ProductionCredentialBroker\n\nSEC-4: RuntimeApprovalProvider — human-in-the-loop approval enforcement\n\n  Flow:\n    PolicyDecision (require_approval)\n      → requestApproval(operation, context)\n      → ApprovalRecord (pending, operationDigest bound)\n      → Human decides: approve / deny / cancel / timeout\n      → verifyApproval(record, operation, context)\n      → VerifiedApproval | ApprovalRejection\n      → execution continues OR fails closed\n\n  Security invariants:\n    - Approval bound to EXACT operation digest (no reuse for modified commands)\n    - Wrong actor cannot approve (identity verified at decide time)\n    - Wrong project/run/tenant fails verification\n    - Expired approval fails\n    - Denied approval never executes\n    - Single-use (scope:once) replay protection\n    - AUTO mode cannot silently bypass (immediate deny)\n    - Headless mode cannot bypass (immediate deny)\n    - Restart discards pending work (no magical approval)\n    - Audit records contain NO credentials/secrets (digest only)\n    - toVerifiedApproval() throws on non-valid results\n\n  Tests: 30 tests, 18 suites — all pass\n\nSEC-5: ProductionCredentialBroker — credential authorization chain\n\n  Flow:\n    VerifiedCapabilityGrant + CredentialRequest\n      → ProductionCredentialBroker.resolve()\n      → CredentialLease (scoped, expiring, revocable)\n      → ProductionCredentialMaterializer.materialize(lease, callback)\n      → MaterializedCredential (available ONLY inside callback)\n      → secret wiped after callback\n\n  Security invariants:\n    - Raw credentials never in grants, leases, events, logs, or audit\n    - Broker accepts CredentialRef, never caller-supplied secret material\n    - Every lease binds: actor, tenant, project, runId, capability, scope, origin\n    - Expired/revoked/wrong-scope leases fail closed\n    - Materialization happens immediately before execution, discarded after\n    - No generic getSecret(name) escape hatch\n    - No agent/model API can enumerate stored secrets\n    - Knowing a credential reference is NEVER enough — lease + verification required\n    - Secret-store outage fails closed\n    - Malformed secret-store response fails closed\n    - Concurrent leases remain isolated\n    - Redaction catches materialized secrets in thrown errors\n    - BYOK credentials cannot leak to other users\n    - Platform credentials respect platform policy\n\n  Pluggable CredentialStore adapter:\n    - InMemoryCredentialStore for testing\n    - Production: Vault, AWS Secrets Manager, Cloudflare Workers Secrets, etc.\n\n  Tests: 33 tests, 26 suites — all pass\n\nFull regression: 438/438 tests pass.\nTypecheck: clean. agent-core build: clean.\n\nGenerated with [Devin](https://devin.ai)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Devin \u003c158243242+devin-ai-integration[bot]@users.noreply.github.com\u003e",
  "Tags": [],
  "Fingerprint": "294814a2f75082eca2eb6b4314dffbf436bc4cd0:packages/litt-agent-core/src/__tests__/sec5-credential-broker.test.ts:generic-api-key:64"
 },
 {
  "RuleID": "generic-api-key",
  "Description": "Detected a Generic API Key, potentially exposing access to various services and sensitive operations.",
  "StartLine": 348,
