  "SymlinkFile": "",
  "Commit": "5e863d848e82f4328a5cd3c3addf1b4f7da035c7",
  "Link": "https://github.com/LabsConnected/litlabs-website/blob/5e863d848e82f4328a5cd3c3addf1b4f7da035c7/packages/litt-cli/src/__tests__/phase3c-agent-loop.test.ts#L372",
  "Entropy": 3.8162405,
  "Author": "Larry B",
  "Email": "highlife4real1989@gmail.com",
  "Date": "2026-08-14T06:34:37Z",
  "Message": "feat(litt-cli): Phase 3C.2 — CLI agent loop through hardened pipeline\n\nCliAgentLoop chains through the existing hardened pipeline:\n\n  CliAgentLoop\n    ↓\n  RuntimeSession.getExecutor()\n    ↓\n  CommandExecutor (hardened execution boundary)\n    ↓\n  runCommand() security boundary (capability classification, approval)\n    ↓\n  ShellExecutor (structured argv, no shell string)\n\nRules enforced:\n  - No spawn/exec/execFile bypass inside the agent loop\n  - Every tool call goes through CommandExecutor → runCommand()\n  - runId stays constant across the entire agent run\n  - Each tool call gets its own toolCallId\n  - Streaming reaches the runtime event bus (tool_stream events)\n  - Cancellation propagates: CLI/runtime → agent loop → CommandExecutor → shell\n  - failed/cancelled/timeout are distinct outcomes\n  - A failed tool call does NOT corrupt the next agent step\n  - Security/approval checks cannot be bypassed because execution\n    originated from an agent\n  - AUTO/ACT/PLAN mode semantics are enforced by runCommand()\n  - No secrets leak into lifecycle events (redactSecrets in runCommand)\n\nApproval integration:\n  - Uses RuntimeApprovalProvider from SEC-4 for cryptographic binding\n  - ACT mode: elevated commands require explicit approval\n  - AUTO mode: elevated auto-approved, dangerous denied (no bypass)\n  - PLAN mode: all mutations rejected\n  - Approval bound to exact operation digest (no reuse for modified commands)\n  - VerifiedApproval promotion via toVerifiedApproval() (only path)\n\nRenamed from AgentLoop to CliAgentLoop to avoid collision with the\nparallel agent's runAgentLoop in agent-core (the model-driven brain).\nThese are complementary:\n  - agent-core runAgentLoop: model → tool call → ToolRegistry\n  - CLI CliAgentLoop: step sequence → CommandExecutor → runCommand()\n\nTests (21 passing):\n  - executes a real tool through CommandExecutor\n  - streaming reaches the agent runtime event bus\n  - cancellation stops the current tool and agent run cleanly\n  - timeout does not become generic failure\n  - failed command can be reasoned about and retried\n  - a failed tool call does not corrupt the next agent step\n  - runId stays constant across the agent run\n  - each tool call gets its own toolCallId\n  - direct execution bypass attempts fail (no shell interpretation)\n  - approval-required action blocks correctly in ACT mode without handler\n  - approval handler denial blocks the command\n  - AUTO mode auto-approves elevated, denies dangerous\n  - PLAN mode rejects mutating, allows read-only\n  - no secrets leak into model/tool lifecycle events\n  - redactStepResult strips secrets from step output\n\nVerification:\n  - CLI build: PASS\n  - CLI tests: 80/80 PASS (3 test files)\n  - agent-core build: PASS\n  - agent-core tests: 405/405 PASS (117 suites)\n  - root typecheck: PASS\n  - terminal-server build: PASS\n\nBoundary respected:\n  - Did NOT modify execution.ts, index.ts (agent-core), command-executor.ts,\n    or Phase 3B tests — parallel agent owns those files\n  - Did NOT touch runtime-client.ts while parallel agent was hardening it\n\nGenerated with [Devin](https://devin.ai)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Devin \u003c158243242+devin-ai-integration[bot]@users.noreply.github.com\u003e",
  "Tags": [],
  "Fingerprint": "5e863d848e82f4328a5cd3c3addf1b4f7da035c7:packages/litt-cli/src/__tests__/phase3c-agent-loop.test.ts:generic-api-key:372"
 },
