 {
  "RuleID": "stripe-access-token",
  "Description": "Found a Stripe Access Token, posing a risk to payment processing services and sensitive financial data.",
  "StartLine": 95,
  "EndLine": 95,
  "StartColumn": 35,
  "EndColumn": 75,
  "Match": "REDACTED\"",
  "Secret": "REDACTED",
  "File": "tests/litt-intelligence-knowledge.test.ts",
  "SymlinkFile": "",
  "Commit": "37ad5a0029d3ea0aa59a8d6e92cf016508e6e5f5",
  "Link": "https://github.com/LabsConnected/litlabs-website/blob/37ad5a0029d3ea0aa59a8d6e92cf016508e6e5f5/tests/litt-intelligence-knowledge.test.ts#L95",
  "Entropy": 4.9341836,
  "Author": "Laid-Back-89",
  "Email": "highlife4real1989@gmail.com",
  "Date": "2026-08-02T19:07:29Z",
  "Message": "Fix Studio chat, auth, voice UI, pricing, and creation tools (#40)\n\n* chore: remove OmniRoute from git index (4,082 files)\n\nOmniRoute was gitignored but never git rm --cached'd, so 4,082\ntracked files remained in the index. This slowed every git operation\nand inflated the TypeScript language server scan.\n\nTracked files: 5,167 -\u003e 1,085 (79% reduction).\n\n* chore: gitignore .worktrees/ and exclude from tsconfig\n\n14 git worktrees were not gitignored or excluded from TypeScript,\ncausing git and the language server to scan 14x source trees.\n\n* fix: correct workspace prepare API path in StudioTerminalDrawer\n\nStudioTerminalDrawer was calling /api/studio-projects/{id}/prepare\nbut the actual route is /api/studio-projects/{id}/workspace/prepare.\nThis caused workspace preparation to silently 404, leaving the\nterminal without a prepared project workspace.\n\n* feat(litt-intelligence): PR 1 — project intelligence scanner\n\nBuild a server-side project scanner that creates a structured\nProjectIntelligenceSnapshot by scanning repository content using\ndeterministic tools (file system reads, manifest parsing, glob\npatterns) — NOT an LLM.\n\nScanner capabilities:\n- Stack detection: languages, frameworks, runtimes, package managers,\n  databases, deployment targets from package.json and config files\n- Architecture detection: entry points, API routes (Next.js App\n  Router), services, data stores, integrations, tool modules\n- Capability detection from file existence (NOT env values) with\n  confidence scores and evidence\n- Dependency analysis from package.json (production/dev/peer/optional)\n- Test inventory: framework detection, test file counting, config path\n- Risk detection: committed .env files, missing .gitignore, deprecated deps\n- Open work detection: recent branches, TODO/FIXME markers\n- Partial scan: re-scan only affected areas when changed files provided\n- Staleness detection: marks snapshot stale when git HEAD changes\n\nScanner rules enforced:\n- Repository content is the source of truth\n- Source paths recorded for every conclusion\n- Confidence scores on every finding\n- Never retrieves or stores secret values\n- Skips generated folders (node_modules, .next, dist, etc.)\n- Does not treat component existence as proof of production-readiness\n- Records scan timestamp and repository SHA\n\nNew files:\n- src/lib/litt-intelligence/types.ts — canonical type definitions\n  for the entire intelligence layer (snapshot, knowledge, research,\n  evaluation, tools, action plans, approvals)\n- src/lib/litt-intelligence/project-scanner.ts — deterministic scanner\n- src/lib/litt-intelligence/index.ts — public API barrel\n- tests/litt-intelligence-scanner.test.ts — 35 tests covering stack,\n  architecture, capabilities, dependencies, tests, risks, staleness,\n  partial scan, secret safety, and skip-dir behavior\n\nExisting architecture reused:\n- Extends src/lib/litt-kernel/ types (TruthClass, CapabilityRecord)\n- Uses same project-scoping pattern as src/lib/studio/project-resolver.ts\n- Follows same secret-detection principle as src/lib/studio/memory-service.ts\n\nNo database changes. No environment variables. No security implications —\nscanner is read-only and never touches secret values.\n\n* feat(litt-intelligence): PR 2 — structured project knowledge\n\nUpgrade memory from conversation-only recall into structured project\nintelligence with 14 knowledge categories, confidence scoring,\nverification status, and supersession tracking.\n\nNew files:\n- supabase/migrations/20260802040000_project_knowledge.sql — table\n  with RLS, indexes, and updated_at trigger\n- src/lib/litt-intelligence/knowledge-service.ts — KnowledgeService\n  class with store, search, get, markStale, markAllStale,\n  updateVerification, answerQuestion, and conflict reconciliation\n- tests/litt-intelligence-knowledge.test.ts — 17 tests covering\n  store, search, get, staleness, verification, question answering,\n  secret blocking, user isolation, and all categories/statuses\n\nKnowledge categories: architecture_fact, dependency_fact,\n  integration_fact, capability_fact, decision, constraint,\n  user_preference, known_issue, failed_attempt, successful_pattern,\n  research_finding, security_risk, release_state, open_question\n\nReconciliation rules:\n- New evidence does NOT overwrite old knowledge silently\n- Old record is marked 'superseded' with superseded_by pointer\n- New record is stored with reference to what it replaced\n- Conversation summaries never outrank repository evidence\n\nDatabase changes:\n- New table: project_knowledge (separate from existing memories)\n- RLS enabled: users can only access their own project knowledge\n- Indexes on owner+project, category, verification_status, updated_at\n\nExisting architecture reused:\n- Same secret detection patterns as memory-service.ts\n- Same Supabase service-role client pattern\n- Same project-scoping principle (owner_id + project_id)\n\nNo environment variables. No security implications — RLS enforced,\nsecrets blocked before storage.\n\n* feat(litt-intelligence): PR 3 — research and discovery engine\n\nCreate a real research engine for current external information with\na provider-based architecture. No hardwired vendor dependency.\n\nNew files:\n- src/lib/litt-intelligence/research-engine.ts — ResearchEngine class\n  with search, fetch, verify, and full research pipeline. Includes\n  planResearchQuery for deterministic query planning and source type\n  ranking (official docs \u003e official repo \u003e API spec \u003e changelog \u003e\n  package registry \u003e maintainer discussion \u003e independent analysis \u003e\n  community discussion)\n- src/lib/litt-intelligence/research-providers.ts — 4 provider\n  implementations:\n    * GitHubSearchProvider — GitHub REST API search (requires GITHUB_TOKEN)\n    * WebSearchProvider — optional SearXNG metasearch backend\n    * PackageRegistryProvider — npm registry search and metadata\n    * OpenAPIDirectoryProvider — APIs.guru OpenAPI discovery catalog\n- tests/litt-intelligence-research.test.ts — 23 tests covering query\n  planning, intent detection, search aggregation, deduplication,\n  source ranking, fetch, verify, full pipeline, and failure handling\n\nProvider interface:\n  interface ResearchProvider {\n    search(query): Promise\u003cSearchResult[]\u003e\n    fetch(source): Promise\u003cFetchedSource | null\u003e\n    verify(source): Promise\u003cVerificationResult\u003e\n  }\n\nSource verification checks:\n- GitHub: valid URL, has content, has README\n- Web: accessible, has content, is official\n- npm: has license, not deprecated, recently updated\n- OpenAPI: valid spec, has paths, has info\n\nOptional providers (behind env vars):\n- SearXNG: SEARXNG_URL\n- Firecrawl: behind provider interface (not yet implemented)\n- GitHub: GITHUB_TOKEN\n\nExisting architecture reused:\n- Same secret-detection patterns\n- Same timeout and error handling patterns\n- Extends types from PR 1 (types.ts)\n\nNo database changes. No security implications — providers are read-only\nand never send credentials to the model.\n\n* feat(litt-intelligence): PR 4 — candidate evaluation and recommendation\n\nCreate a consistent candidate-scoring model across 15 evaluation\ndimensions with evidence-backed scores and weighted overall scoring.\n\nNew files:\n- src/lib/litt-intelligence/evaluator.ts — CandidateEvaluator class\n  with evaluate() for single candidates and recommend() for multi-\n  candidate comparison. Security and compatibility weighted higher.\n- tests/litt-intelligence-evaluator.test.ts — 19 tests covering\n  dimensions, evaluation, recommendation, integration plans, risk\n  collection, weighted scoring, and all candidate types\n\n15 evaluation dimensions:\n  project_compatibility, implementation_effort, operational_cost,\n  license_compatibility, security_risk, maintenance_health,\n  api_quality, documentation_quality, vendor_lock_in,\n  self_hosting_difficulty, performance, reliability, user_privacy,\n  commercial_use_suitability, reversibility\n\nRecommendation types: use existing, extend existing, adopt open-source,\n  integrate API, self-host, build internally, postpone, reject\n\nIntegration plans include: steps, files to create/modify, dependencies,\n  estimated effort, and rollback plan.\n\nApproval required for: API and self-hosted candidates.\nNo approval for: internal builds, postpone, reject.\n\nNo database changes. No environment variables. No security implications.\n\n* feat(litt-intelligence): PR 5 — tool registry and MCP/OpenAPI adapters\n\nCreate a canonical tool registry owned by the LiTT Kernel. Every\nexecutable tool declares its schema, risk, approval policy, and\npermissions. MCP and OpenAPI tools pass the same validation as\ninternal tools and can never bypass the permission system.\n\nNew files:\n- src/lib/litt-intelligence/tool-registry.ts — ToolRegistry singleton\n  with 20 internal tools (read-only and mutation), validation,\n  execution, quarantine, and change notifications\n- src/lib/litt-intelligence/mcp-adapter.ts — MCPAdapter for\n  connecting to approved MCP servers and converting their tools\n- src/lib/litt-intelligence/openapi-adapter.ts — OpenAPIAdapter for\n  parsing OpenAPI specs, validating safety, and generating tools\n- tests/litt-intelligence-tool-registry.test.ts — 39 tests covering\n  tool registration, enable/disable, quarantine, validation,\n  execution, canExecute, change listeners, MCP adapter, and\n  OpenAPI adapter\n\nInternal tools registered:\n  Read-only: project.scan, project.read_context, memory.search,\n    web.search, web.fetch, github.search_code, github.read_file,\n    github.list_pull_requests, github.inspect_workflow,\n    api.search_openapi, package.inspect, files.list, files.read\n  Mutations: image.generate, files.write, files.patch,\n    checkpoint.create, checkpoint.restore, preview.open,\n    memory.store, approval.request\n  Disabled: terminal.execute (Coming Soon, neverAllow)\n\nMCP adapter rules:\n- Only approved servers can register\n- Tools must be in allowed list\n- Quarantined tools are never-allow\n- Default risk: medium (unknown provenance)\n\nOpenAPI adapter rules:\n- Rejects external  references\n- Rejects disallowed server hosts\n- GET operations: read-only, auto-approve\n- POST/PUT/PATCH/DELETE: mutation, explicit approval required\n- Deprecated operations: disabled by default\n\nNo database changes. No environment variables. Security: MCP tools\nand OpenAPI tools cannot bypass approval system.\n\n* feat(connectors): provider registry, DB schema, repository, and types\n\n- Add provider-registry.ts with platform/user provider definitions\n- Add connector-repository.ts for user connections CRUD\n- Add db-types.ts matching the migration schema\n- Add migration for connector tables with RLS\n- Extend integration types with personal connector categories\n\n* feat(litt-intelligence): user context, permission gate, weather tool\n\n- user-context.ts: aggregates user profile, preferences, location,\n  and capability statuses into a single UserContext object\n- permission-gate.ts: enforces consent checks before any connector\n  tool call; fails honestly when permission is missing\n- weather-provider.ts: Open-Meteo API integration (no API key needed)\n  with geocode, current, hourly, and daily forecast endpoints\n- weather-tool.ts: combines user context + permission gate + weather\n  provider into a single callable tool with formatted output\n- 22 tests covering all layers (unit + mocked fetch)\n\n* feat(intelligence): API routes for weather, context, permissions + wire to LiTT think\n\n- GET /api/intelligence/weather — fetch current/hourly/daily weather\n- GET /api/intelligence/context — get user context (profile, prefs, caps)\n- POST /api/intelligence/permissions — grant/revoke capability consent\n- LiTT think route now detects personal-assistant queries (weather,\n  temperature, forecast, rain) and routes them through the weather\n  tool with user context + permission gate\n\n* docs: add repo performance baseline measurements\n\n* perf: exclude .worktrees from git, TypeScript, ESLint, and Vitest\n\n- .gitignore: add .worktrees/ (376K files were visible to git)\n- tsconfig.json: add .worktrees to exclude (was scanning 376K extra files)\n- eslint.config.mjs: add .worktrees, coverage, test-results,\n  playwright-report, docs to globalIgnores (lint was 602s / 10 min)\n- vitest.config.ts: add .worktrees, test-results, playwright-report,\n  coverage to exclude\n- git rm --cached OmniRoute (4,082 tracked files removed from index)\n\n* docs: add agent fast workflow guide\n\n* docs: add repo performance final report\n\n- Lint: 602.8s -\u003e 42.0s (93% improvement, 14x faster)\n- TSC: 33.6s -\u003e 11.0s (67% improvement, 3x faster)\n- Tests: 40s/700 -\u003e 23.3s/518 (42% faster, OmniRoute excluded)\n- Build: 47s -\u003e 47s (no change, already clean)\n- No production changes, no secrets exposed, no merge to main\n\n* fix: break infinite re-render loop on /studio (React error #185 + #310)\n\nRoot cause: loadConversations depended on searchParams, creating a feedback\ncycle: loadConversations → selectConversation → syncUrl → router.replace →\nsearchParams change → loadConversations re-runs → infinite loop.\n\nTwo fixes:\n1. Guard selectConversation in useConversationStore to not emit when\n   the conversation id hasn't changed (prevents unnecessary store updates)\n2. Use a ref for searchParams in loadConversations so it only re-runs\n   when serverProjectId or userId changes, not on every URL change\n   (URL→state sync is already handled by the separate URL sync effect)\n\n* stabilize production landing and deployment\n\n* fix: resolve React error #418 on /marketplace + stabilize Zustand selectors\n\nTwo fixes for intermittent 'Something went wrong' crashes:\n\n1. Marketplace hydration mismatch (#418): useSearchParams() in useState initializer produced different server/client render output. Moved the searchParams read into a useEffect so initial state is consistent.\n\n2. Zustand selector returning fresh [] (React 19 #185): useSyncExternalStore saw a new array identity on every snapshot, causing 'Maximum update depth exceeded' before conversation data loaded. Replaced with a shared EMPTY_CONVERSATION_MESSAGES constant.\n\nAlso: gitignore .codex-deploy-stage-* and .codex-prod logs.\n\nGenerated with [Devin](https://devin.ai)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Devin \u003c158243242+devin-ai-integration[bot]@users.noreply.github.com\u003e\n\n* fix: stabilize studio selectors and ship current snapshot\n\n* feat(music-lab): port Music Lab into CommandStudio architecture\n\nPort the Music Lab from feat/music-lab-import into the current production\nCommandStudio architecture WITHOUT merging the deprecated StudioOS shell.\n\nLibrary/providers/types/hooks (reusable, deps verified against prod):\n- src/types/music.ts, src/lib/music/{generation-service,safety-filter}.ts\n- src/lib/music/providers/{index,factory,mock,mureka,elevenlabs,http}.ts\n- src/hooks/use-music-{generation,vault}.ts + generation-service.test.ts\n\nAPI routes (net-new; /api/music/generate kept as legacy MiniMax proxy):\n- POST /api/music/generations (async, billed, idempotent) + status/cancel\n- GET/PATCH/DELETE /api/music/tracks + GET .../stream\n- Mock gated to tests/dev via isMockAllowed(); rate-limited + structured logs\n\nCommandStudio integration (no second shell):\n- Add 'music' to StudioTool union; route create/music -\u003e MusicTool\n- Register MusicTool in TOOL_COMPONENTS; createTabs already had Music\n- Updated destination tests music-\u003emusic (was placeholder music-\u003eaudio)\n\nMigration: 20260802050000_music_lab_tables.sql (renumbered from\n20260730000000 to avoid collision with premium_agents_v1_port); fully\nidempotent, deny-all RLS + service-role-only access, FK to public.users.\n\n* fix: add missing Vercel build compatibility stub\n\n* fix: make studio chat show immediately on send\n\n* chore: exclude local worktrees from vercel uploads\n\n* fix: stabilize studio auth voice and creation UI\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Devin \u003c158243242+devin-ai-integration[bot]@users.noreply.github.com\u003e",
  "Tags": [],
  "Fingerprint": "37ad5a0029d3ea0aa59a8d6e92cf016508e6e5f5:tests/litt-intelligence-knowledge.test.ts:stripe-access-token:95"
